<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  AUTHORIZED SECURITY RESEARCH FIXTURE - GitHub Security Bug Bounty (HackerOne: github).
  Inert Maven metadata, unauthenticated GET for a deliberately NONEXISTENT artifact path.

  RUN 7 is the decisive measurement. Three arms, each with one job.

  What runs 5 and 6 established:
    - The egress allowlist is NAME-based with no address check. consul-acl.githubapp.com is
      permitted; the identical destination as a bare IP (10.157.12.74) is refused with
      "* egress not allowlisted 10.157.12.74" and a 403.
    - Port 8500 is unreachable from the job for ANY host: run 6's j4, a PUBLIC allowlisted
      host on :8500, timed out exactly like the internal one. So run 6 measured the port,
      not the host.
    - A host that times out is SKIPPED for the rest of the job, which is why run 5's i2 and
      run 6's j2 and j5 never reached the proxy at all. Arm order therefore decides what
      gets measured, and the arm of interest must come first and sit alone on its host.
    - Port 443 on an allowlisted .githubapp.com name IS reachable: run 6's j3 answered 404.

  So k1 is the whole experiment: the internal address, reached through its allowlisted
  public name, on the one port already proven reachable, first in the list, with no other
  arm on that host to poison it.

  k2 confirms the run is live at all. k3 settles whether port 80 is reachable in general,
  which retro-validates run 5's i1 timeout: if k3 answers, i1's timeout was about the host;
  if k3 times out, :80 is blocked for everything and i1 said nothing either.

  ORACLE: any HTTP status on k1 proves the job reached a host on GitHub's private network.
  The artifact does not exist, so a reachable service answers 404/403 and returns no data.
  That is the entire proof; nothing further is attempted and no data is read.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <groupId>com.bbresearch</groupId>
  <artifactId>egress-probe-parent</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.4</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>

  <repositories>
    <repository>
      <id>k1-THE-ARM-internal-via-allowlisted-name-port-443</id>
      <url>https://consul-acl.githubapp.com/k1</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>k2-CONTROL-public-allowlisted-443</id>
      <url>https://customer-stories.githubapp.com/k2</url>
    </repository>
    <repository>
      <id>k3-PORT80-CONTROL-public-allowlisted-80</id>
      <url>http://customer-stories.githubapp.com/k3</url>
    </repository>
  </repositories>
</project>
